 "title": "Building Department - Welcome to Alcona County",
 "text": "Building Department - Welcome to Alcona County\nSkip to content\nMenu\nAlcona Home\nAlcona County Trial Court\n23rd Circuit Court\n81st District Court\nFriend of the Court\nJuvenile Court\nProbate Court\nRecovery Court\nDepartments\nBuilding Department\nCounty Clerk\nCounty Commissioners\nCounty Treasurer\nEqualization Department\nGrounds and Maintenance\nProsecuting Attorney\nRegister of Deeds\nSheriff’s Department\n911 Central Dispatch\nVeterans Affairs\nJob Postings\nCitizen Information\nALCONA-ECONOMIC DEVELOPMENT COMMITTEE (A-EDC)\nAccountability and Transparency in Government\nCounty Directory\nCourthouse – Hours of Operation\nEducation\nAlcona Community Schools\nFairview Area Schools\nOscoda Area Schools\nAlpena-Montmorency-Alcona Educational Service District\nCounty Services\nAlcona Conservation District\nAlcona County Commission On Aging\nAlcona County Library\nDistrict Health Department #2\nEmergency Medical Services\nHousing Commission\nMSU Extension\nTownship Information\nTownship Officials\nTownship Websites\nAlcona Township\nCalendonia Township\nCurtis Township\nGustin Township\nGreenbush Township\nCity of Harrisville\nHarrisville Township\nHawes Township\nVillage of Lincoln\nMillen Township\nMitchell Township\nArea Information\nAlcona County Chamber of Commerce\nAlcona County Fair\nAlcona County Quilt Trail\nAlcona Recycling\nHuron Pines Resource Conservation and Development\nMichigan Works\nNortheast Michigan Council of Governments\nNortheast Michigan Community Service Agency\nState of Michigan (Department of Human Services)\nState of Michigan (Department of Natural Resources)\nU.S. 23 Heritage Route\nSearch\nSearch field required\nSearch\nWelcome To Alcona County\nBuilding Department\nBuilding Dept. Forms\nInspection FAQ\nBuilding Dept. Permits\nBuilding Department\nBuilding Department\nThe Alcona County Building Division is dedicated to ensuring public safety in all construction and development projects within our community. We achieve this by enforcing building codes and zoning ordinances, and meticulously maintaining records related to the construction, alteration, and demolition of buildings and structures.\nAs mandated by Michigan State law in 2004, Alcona County has adopted and enforces the Michigan Building Code and the Michigan Residential Code. These codes establish minimum requirements to protect public health, safety, and general welfare. This includes addressing structural strength, safe exits, stability, sanitation, adequate light and ventilation, energy conservation, and protection from fire and other hazards. These codes also prioritize the safety of firefighters and emergency responders during operations.\nThe Alcona County Building Division is committed to serving our community. We strive to provide an efficient and user-friendly permitting process while maintaining accurate records. Our goal is to contribute to a high standard of living for all residents of Alcona County.\n216 W. Main Street\nHarrisville, MI 48740\nPhone (989) 724-9440 / Fax (989) 724-9449\nOffice Hours\nMonday-Friday 8:30am - Noon and 1:00pm - 4:30pm\nClosed Legal & County Holidays\nBuilding Department\nPermits\nPay Online\nGet In Touch!\n216 W. Main Street\nHarrisville, MI 48740\n989-724-9440\n989-724-9449\nJennifer Maynard\nBuilding Department Clerk\nDan Gauthier\nBuilding Department Director\n989-724-9442\nJohn Jagelewski\nPlumbing & Mechanical Inspector\n989-724-9440\nHarry Harvey\nBuilding Inspector\n989-724-9440\nJoshua A. Schaeffer\nElectrical Inspector\n989-724-9440\n© 2026 Welcome to Alcona County. All Rights Reserved.\nScroll To Top",
